# Credential Guard — Shared Allowlist
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is read by scripts/hooks/credential-guard BEFORE a hit is
# reported, so entries here prevent false-positive blocks. Keep this file
# conservative. Every entry is an explicit exception to the gate.
#
# Format (one rule per line; lines starting with `#` are comments):
#
#   string:LITERAL        exact substring match — anywhere it appears, the
#                         line is treated as allowed.
#
#   regex:/ERE/           POSIX extended regular expression. The surrounding
#                         slashes are optional but recommended for clarity.
#                         GNU/BSD grep both support `-E`.
#
#   path:GLOB             glob matching the staged file path. Useful for
#                         docs, samples, and test fixtures. `**` means
#                         "any number of path components".
#
# IMPORTANT — placeholder strings are dangerous to commit. Many vendors
# (GitHub, Stripe, AWS, …) use a fixed prefix + 24-40 alphanum characters
# for their real keys. A placeholder that is shaped like a real key
# (e.g. a Stripe test prefix followed by 24 X characters) will itself
# match a real-key regex, so GitHub's push protection will refuse the
# push. If you need a placeholder for documentation or seed code, break
# the alphanum run with a non-alphanumeric character (underscore,
# angle brackets, etc.). Example shape:
#
#   # GOOD — angle brackets break the run, scanner does not match
#   string:sk_test_<replace-with-real-test-key>
#   string:ghp_<replace-with-real-github-pat>
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Documentation & examples ----------------------------------------------
# Markdown files under docs/ are documentation. Placeholder keys in
# prose are normal here and should not block.
path:docs/**/*.md
path:docs/**/*.MD

# ---- Sample / fixture files -----------------------------------------------
# Common sample locations.
path:**/samples/**
path:**/Samples/**
path:**/fixtures/**
path:**/*.example.json
path:**/*.example.yaml
path:**/*.example.yml
path:**/*.example.cs

# ---- Test code -------------------------------------------------------------
# Test projects frequently contain literal "secret-looking" strings used
# to assert behaviour. Allowlist them by convention.
path:**/tests/**
path:**/*.Tests/**

# ---- Credential Guard self-bootstrap ---------------------------------------
# The implementation file (credential-guard) MUST contain example secret
# strings in its self-test fixtures and as part of the pattern definitions.
# Without these entries, the hook would block its own source commit —
# a classic bootstrap problem. The path rule bypasses both the path-block
# check and the content scan for these two files.
path:scripts/hooks/credential-guard
path:scripts/hooks/credential-guard.allowlist

# ---- Add your team's own rules below --------------------------------------
# Examples (delete these before committing; they are illustrative only):
#
#   # Test fixture for the auth integration test:
#   string:sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx_PLACEHOLDER
#
#   # A specific config file that legitimately contains env-var names:
#   path:config/local.example.yaml
